  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "This paper presents a bibliometric and systematic literature review of bus lane research spanning from 1969 to 2024. It maps out publication distributions, key contributors, and prominent themes, categorizing the existing body of work into four core domains: design and planning, operational efficiency evaluation, broader societal and environmental impacts, and integrated operational strategies.",
      "why": "It synthesizes over five decades of fragmented transportation research into a structured taxonomy, establishing a baseline of historical trends and current knowledge boundaries for transit planners and researchers."
